<title>USA: Duke Catawba S.C. nuke resumes full power.</title>
<headline>Duke Catawba S.C. nuke resumes full power.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duke Power Co's 1,129 megawatt (MW) Catawba 2 nuclear unit has returned to full power Friday, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said in its plant status report.</p>
<p>The unit, in Clover, S.C., has been operating between 60 and 70 percent power since this weekend due to a condenser tube leak and a valve failure.</p>
<p>Catawba 1, also 1,129 MW, was running at full power.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
</text>
